  "presentation_summary": [
    "23-year-old previously healthy Taiwanese male soldier developed right otalgia and 11 days of intermittent fever up to 39 degC after jungle training.",
    "He initially received amoxicillin-clavulanate for presumed otitis but fever persisted.",
    "By illness day 6 he developed generalized maculopapular rash, cramping abdominal pain, and watery diarrhea; during the 4 days before referral he developed progressive dyspnea and cough.",
    "Examination showed cardiopulmonary distress, icteric sclera, external auditory canal eschar, and bilateral basal rales.",
    "Laboratory findings showed severe thrombocytopenia, hepatitis/cholestasis, high CRP, high LDH, hypoalbuminemia, and mild AKI; chest radiograph showed bilateral diffuse infiltrates consistent with ARDS.",
    "Weil-Felix OX-K was positive and he defervesced after doxycycline."
  ],
